<p>Relative speed = 50 + 70 = 120 km/h</p>

<p><b>Step 2:</b></p>
<p>Change in distance = 120 × 2</p>

<p><b>Step 3:</b></p>
<p>Change in distance = <b>240 km</b></p>

<h3>Worked Example 3</h3>

<p>
A motorcycle travels at 45 km/h while a car ahead travels at 30 km/h.
How much closer does the motorcycle get in 4 hours?
</p>

<p><b>Step 1:</b></p>
<p>Relative speed = 45 − 30 = 15 km/h</p>

<p><b>Step 2:</b></p>
<p>Change in distance = 15 × 4</p>

<p><b>Answer = 60 km</b></p>
