<h2>Finding the Meeting Point</h2>

<p>
After finding the meeting time, the meeting position can be found by using:
</p>

<p>
<b>Distance travelled = speed × time</b>
</p>

<p>
The distance travelled by either object from its own starting point is its
distance to the meeting point.
</p>

<h3>Worked Example 1</h3>

<p>
Two cars are 180 km apart. They travel towards each other at 60 km/h and
30 km/h and meet after 2 hours.
Find the distance travelled by the first car.
</p>

<p>
Distance = speed × time
</p>

<p>
d = 60 × 2
</p>

<p>
<b>d = 120 km</b>
</p>

<p>
Therefore the meeting point is 120 km from the first town.
</p>

<h3>Worked Example 2</h3>

<p>
Two cyclists are 100 km apart. One travels at 20 km/h and the other at
30 km/h. They meet after 2 hours.
