Distance travelled by first cyclist:
</p>

<p>
20 × 2 = <b>40 km</b>
</p>

<p>
So they meet 40 km from the first cyclist''s starting point.
</p>

<h3>Worked Example 3</h3>

<p>
Two buses are 300 km apart. The first travels at 80 km/h and they meet
after 2 hours.
</p>

<p>
Meeting distance from the first bus:
</p>

<p>
80 × 2 = <b>160 km</b>
</p>
