<h2>Forming a Revenue Objective Function</h2>

<p>
<b>Revenue</b> is the total money received from selling products.
</p>

<p>
Revenue is calculated by:
</p>

<p>
<b>Revenue = selling price per unit × number of units</b>
</p>

<p>
When there are two products, add their revenues.
</p>

<h3>Example 1</h3>

<p>
A shop sells shirts for KSh 1,000 each and trousers for KSh 1,500 each.
</p>

<p>
Let:
</p>

<p>
x = number of shirts<br>
y = number of trousers
</p>

<p>
Shirt revenue:
</p>

<p>
1000x
</p>

<p>
Trouser revenue:
</p>

<p>
1500y
</p>

<p>
Therefore:
</p>

<p>
<b>R = 1000x + 1500y</b>
</p>

<h3>Example 2</h3>

<p>
A farmer sells maize at KSh 3,000 per bag and beans at KSh 4,000
per bag.
</p>

<p>
Let x = bags of maize and y = bags of beans.
</p>

<p>
Revenue:
</p>

<p>
<b>R = 3000x + 4000y</b>
</p>

<h3>Example 3</h3>

<p>
A bakery sells bread at KSh 70 per loaf and cakes at KSh 300 each.
If x loaves and y cakes are sold:
</p>

<p>
Bread revenue = 70x
</p>

<p>
Cake revenue = 300y
</p>

<p>
Therefore:
</p>

<p>
<b>R = 70x + 300y</b>
</p>

<p>
If the aim is to obtain the greatest sales income:
</p>

<p>
<b>Maximize R = 70x + 300y</b>
</p>
