<h2>Building a Linear Programming Model from a Complete Problem</h2>

<p>
This screen combines the translation skills without yet solving the
model graphically.
</p>

<h3>Problem</h3>

<p>
A bakery makes bread and cakes.
</p>

<p>
Each loaf of bread requires 2 hours of labour and each cake requires
3 hours.
The bakery has at most 60 labour hours.
</p>

<p>
The bakery must make at least 10 cakes and loaves altogether.
</p>

<p>
The profit is KSh 40 per loaf and KSh 100 per cake.
The bakery wants to maximize profit.
</p>

