<p>
Bread uses 2x hours.
</p>

<p>
Cakes use 3y hours.
</p>

<p>
Total labour:
</p>

<p>
2x + 3y
</p>

<p>
At most 60:
</p>

<p>
<b>2x + 3y ≤ 60</b>
</p>

<h3>Step 3: Translate minimum production</h3>

<p>
Total products:
</p>

<p>
x + y
</p>

<p>
At least 10:
</p>

<p>
<b>x + y ≥ 10</b>
</p>

<h3>Step 4: Non-negativity</h3>

<p>
<b>x ≥ 0, y ≥ 0</b>
</p>

<h3>Step 5: Form the objective</h3>

<p>
Bread profit:
</p>

<p>
40x
</p>

<p>
Cake profit:
</p>

<p>
100y
</p>

<p>
Therefore:
</p>

<p>
<b>Maximize P = 40x + 100y</b>
</p>

