  (216, 216, '
<h2>Finding Mean Using Σfx ÷ Σf</h2>

<p>
Once a frequency table has been created, we can find the mean without
writing every repeated value.
</p>

<p>
The formula is:
</p>

<p>
<b>Mean = Σfx ÷ Σf</b>
</p>

<p>
where:
</p>

<ul>
<li><b>Σfx</b> = total of all fx values.</li>
<li><b>Σf</b> = total frequency, or total number of observations.</li>
</ul>

<h3>Worked Example 1</h3>

<table>
<tr><th>x</th><th>f</th><th>fx</th></tr>
<tr><td>2</td><td>3</td><td>6</td></tr>
<tr><td>4</td><td>2</td><td>8</td></tr>
</table>

<p>
First find Σfx:
</p>

<p>
Σfx = 6 + 8 = <b>14</b>
</p>

<p>
Then find Σf:
</p>

<p>
Σf = 3 + 2 = <b>5</b>
</p>

<p>
Therefore:
</p>

<p>
Mean = 14 ÷ 5
</p>

<p>
Mean = <b>2.8</b>
</p>

<h3>Worked Example 2</h3>

<table>
<tr><th>x</th><th>f</th><th>fx</th></tr>
<tr><td>5</td><td>2</td><td>10</td></tr>
<tr><td>10</td><td>3</td><td>30</td></tr>
<tr><td>15</td><td>1</td><td>15</td></tr>
</table>

<p>
Σfx = 10 + 30 + 15 = <b>55</b>
</p>

<p>
Σf = 2 + 3 + 1 = <b>6</b>
</p>

<p>
Mean = 55 ÷ 6
</p>

<p>
Mean = <b>9.17</b> approximately.
</p>

<h3>Worked Example 3</h3>

<table>
<tr><th>x</th><th>f</th><th>fx</th></tr>
<tr><td>3</td><td>4</td><td>12</td></tr>
<tr><td>6</td><td>2</td><td>12</td></tr>
<tr><td>9</td><td>4</td><td>36</td></tr>
</table>

<p>
Σfx:
</p>

<p>
12 + 12 + 36 = <b>60</b>
</p>

<p>
Σf:
</p>

<p>
4 + 2 + 4 = <b>10</b>
</p>

<p>
Mean:
</p>

<p>
60 ÷ 10 = <b>6</b>
</p>

<h3>Memory rule</h3>

<p>
Do not confuse the two totals:
</p>

<p>
<b>Σfx = total of the data values.</b>
</p>

<p>
<b>Σf = number of observations.</b>
</p>

<p>
Then:
</p>

<p>
<b>Mean = Σfx ÷ Σf</b>
</p>
