  (2033, 476, 'What is the role of saliva in taste?', 'text', 1, 'Focus on the core principle of The Tongue (Structure, Function & Taste Process).', '{"why":"Without saliva, taste is reduced","sol":"Step 1: Identify key concept: Define the required principles for The Tongue (Structure, Function & Taste Process).\nStep 2: Apply governing rule: Without saliva, taste is reduced\nStep 3: State the final conclusion: It dissolves food chemicals so taste buds can detect them","steps":["Step 1: Identify key concept: Define the required principles for The Tongue (Structure, Function & Taste Process).","Step 2: Apply governing rule: Without saliva, taste is reduced","Step 3: State the final conclusion: It dissolves food chemicals so taste buds can detect them"],"options":[],"conceptId":"biology_nervous_system_the_tongue_structure_function_taste_process","skillId":"biology_nervous_system","subskillId":"biology_nervous_system_q3","subject":"biology","chapter":"nervous_system","topic":"The Tongue (Structure, Function & Taste Process)"}', 2),
